{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016RJLNsnkKL9kXezhEP9R8u","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-prod43/projects/gated_mfrm_judge_bias/literature_map.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meta:\\\\n  last_updated: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n  total_papers: 12\\\\ncategories:\\\\n  - key: \\\\\\\"psychometric_foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    name: \\\\\\\"Psychometric & IRT Foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative: \\\\\\\"Core psychometric models: DG-IRT gating mechanism for cheating detection, MFRM applied to LLM raters, and IRT-based LLM evaluation frameworks\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - key: \\\\\\\"judge_bias_correction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    name: \\\\\\\"Judge Bias Correction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative: \\\\\\\"Methods for detecting and correcting systematic biases in LLM-as-a-judge evaluation pipelines\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - key: \\\\\\\"contamination_detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n    name: \\\\\\\"Contamination Detection & Adjustment\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative: \\\\\\\"Methods for detecting and quantifying benchmark contamination in LLM evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - key: \\\\\\\"unified_evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    name: \\\\\\\"Unified Evaluation Frameworks\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative: \\\\\\\"Comprehensive LLM evaluation frameworks and benchmarks that combine multiple assessment dimensions\\\\\\\"\\\\npapers:\\\\n  shu2013dgirt:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Using Deterministic, Gated Item Response Theory Model to Detect Test Cheating due to Item Compromise\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Shu, Z.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Henson, R.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Luecht, R.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2013\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"Psychometrika\\\\\\\"\\\\n    doi: \\\\\\\"10.1007/s11336-012-9311-3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"shu2013dgirt\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"psychometric_foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Core methodological inspiration. DG-IRT decomposes observed performance into genuine ability and cheating-inflated components via a gating mechanism. G-MFRM adapts this gating logic from educational cheating to LLM benchmark contamination.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  wang2025mfrm_llm:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Comparing Human and AI Rater Effects Using the Many-Facet Rasch Model\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Wang, Y.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2505.18486\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"wang2025mfrm_llm\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"psychometric_foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Most direct predecessor. Applies MFRM to compare 10 LLM raters with human experts, demonstrating MFRM's applicability to LLM judge calibration. Does NOT model contamination — the gap G-MFRM fills.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  lin2025psnirt:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Lost in Benchmarks? Rethinking LLM Benchmarking with IRT — PSN-IRT\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Lin, Z.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"AAAI\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"lin2025psnirt\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"psychometric_foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Neural 4PL IRT for LLM benchmark evaluation. Demonstrates scalability of IRT to LLMs but lacks judge facet and contamination modeling. Serves as IRT-based baseline without multi-facet structure.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  cyclicjudge2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"CyclicJudge: Mitigating Judge Bias Efficiently in LLM-based Evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Unknown\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"cyclicjudge2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"judge_bias_correction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Primary bias-only baseline. Eliminates judge bias via round-robin assignment but completely ignores contamination. G-MFRM addresses both jointly.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  fiedler2026bias_uncertainty:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Bias and Uncertainty in LLM-as-a-Judge Estimation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Fiedler, M.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2605.06939\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"fiedler2026bias_uncertainty\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"judge_bias_correction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"related\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Introduces formal J/delta-J diagnostics for judge bias, identifies sign-reversal failure modes in shared-calibration comparisons. Stays within classical test theory. G-MFRM's confounding argument positions Fiedler's sign-reversal as downstream consequence of unmodeled contamination.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  soumik2026judging_judges:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Judging the Judges: Systematic Evaluation of Bias Mitigation Strategies in LLM-as-a-Judge Pipelines\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Soumik, M.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    arxiv_id: \\\\\\\"2604.23178\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"soumik2026judging_judges\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"judge_bias_correction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"related\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Empirically compares 9 debiasing strategies across 5 judges, finding style bias dominant (0.76-0.92). Provides no measurement model explaining why strategies work — G-MFRM provides the explanatory framework.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  uda2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"UDA: Unsupervised Debiasing Alignment for LLM Judges\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Unknown\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"AAAI\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"uda2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"judge_bias_correction\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Neural K-factor adjustment reducing inter-judge std by 63.4%. Black-box neural approach vs G-MFRM's interpretable psychometric approach. Key baseline for judge bias correction.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  constat2024:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"ConStat: Statistical Detection and Quantification of Benchmark Contamination\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Unknown\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"constat2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"contamination_detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Core component of G-MFRM Stage 2. Computes contamination effects via reference benchmark comparison (r^2=0.94 with true effects). Fully black-box, used to estimate per-item exposure e_i.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  dcr2025:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"DCR: Quantifying Data Contamination in LLMs Evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Unknown\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2025\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"EMNLP\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"dcr2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"contamination_detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"baseline\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Adjusts accuracy for contamination via fuzzy inference but ignores judge effects. Primary contamination-only baseline for G-MFRM comparison.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  preference_leakage2026:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Preference Leakage: A Contamination Problem in LLM-as-a-judge\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Unknown\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2026\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"ICLR\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"preference_leakage2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"contamination_detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"related\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Quantifies generator-judge relatedness bias (judge-side contamination). Distinct from G-MFRM's examinee-side contamination. Preference Leakage's relatedness bias can be partially captured by G-MFRM's d_j facet.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  logprober2024:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"LogProber: Detecting Data Contamination via Token Log-Probability Analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Unknown\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2024\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"arXiv\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"logprober2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"contamination_detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"component\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Estimates per-item Safe Scores from token log-probabilities. Gray-box exposure indicator for G-MFRM Stage 2 (for models exposing logprobs).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  zheng2023mtbench:\\\\n    title: \\\\\\\"Judging LLM-as-a-Judge with MT-Bench and Chatbot Arena\\\\\\\"\\\\n    authors:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Zheng, L.\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Chiang, W.-L.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    year: 2023\\\\n    venue: \\\\\\\"NeurIPS\\\\\\\"\\\\n    bibtex_key: \\\\\\\"zheng2023mtbench\\\\\\\"\\\\n    category: \\\\\\\"unified_evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    role: \\\\\\\"foundation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    relevance: \\\\\\\"Establishes LLM-as-a-judge paradigm and MT-Bench/Chatbot Arena benchmarks. Primary evaluation benchmark for G-MFRM validation. Human votes from Arena serve as ground truth for Kendall-tau comparison.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    verified: false\\\\n    added_by: \\\\\\\"director\\\\\\\"\\\\n    added_at: \\\\\\\"2026-05-21T16:40:00Z\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 7733, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01A1TLRBFFn17v4XNYciSLcZ","session_id":"7b85d8bd-7258-4dfd-917f-e95cb5e144aa","uuid":"9ef49fdc-4d62-41c2-9d7c-4c877fc0d3e0","timestamp":"2026-05-21T21:18:33.195Z"}
